# `@korvyn/core`

Read [`packages/core/README.md`](../../packages/core/README.md) before editing — it is the
full working guide. [`packages/core/CLAUDE.md`](../../packages/core/CLAUDE.md) is the
load-bearing summary.

A typed GAAP domain model (`src/domain` — accounts, entities, dimensions, periods, journal
entries, validation) plus the adapter seam (`src/integration`). Also the CIP→PIS
capital-asset lifecycle (`src/domain/capital.ts`) and a validated multinational GL fixture
(`src/fixtures/enterprise-gl.ts`). No sync engine, no persistence, no real API calls, no
UI — deliberately.

## Must not break

- **The boundary is one-directional.** `integration/` may import `domain/`, never the
  reverse. **No vendor field name** (NetSuite / Intacct / Yardi / Procore / QuickBooks …)
  may appear outside an adapter's private translation code. `tools/check_boundary.py`
  enforces this without Node — run it.
- **Vocabulary is GAAP's, not any vendor's.** Translation is an adapter's job.
- Modelling a journal entry is not posting one. The ERP stays the system of record.

## Check

```bash
cd packages/core && npm run check   # typecheck + typecheck:test + tests + boundary checker
```

Node is not on `PATH` — see the project rule.
